{
  "name": "Prism Line (3 band)",
  "notes": "Port of `prism_line`. THREE LINES ON ONE SINE PATH, which is the entire animation and which the previous port did not have at all -- it pushed three centres apart with audio and never swung them.\n\nOne `lfo(sine)` is the path and every layer reads it, so the colours agree about WHEN to swing and disagree only about HOW FAR. Superimposed they sum toward white -- `add`, and not divided by the colour count, because an overlap is supposed to be bright -- and they separate into a spectrum as their amplitudes diverge. That is why the palette is primaries: red, green and blue at the same place are exactly white.\n\nEACH LAYER'S AMPLITUDE IS THREE ROWS ON ITS CENTRE, and they are three because a row has one source and an amplitude is a PRODUCT of the oscillator with a level:\n  `M4 * 0.02`         the swing that is there in silence -- `amp_min`\n  `M5 * 0.21`         `math(mul, sine, overall)`: every colour rides the overall level\n  `M6..8 * 0.12`      `math(mul, sine, own band)`: this colour rides its own slice\nSummed, that is `sin * (amp_min + overall*a + rel_i*b)` -- the animation's split blend with the loudness weighting held fixed. The animation makes the blend factor `overall * split_depth`, so how much the colours are ALLOWED to disagree itself depends on how loud it is; that is quadratic in the bands and would cost two more math nodes than the rack has room for. What survives is the part that reads: quiet is a narrow white line, loud is a wide fractured one.\n\n`split_depth` therefore lands on the three slice bands' `sensitivity` rather than on a blend factor. More gain on a colour's own band is more disagreement, which is the knob's meaning even though it is not its arithmetic.\n\nTEN BANDS BECOME THREE, the same gap `09-fft-bars` has: `SpectrumSignal` gives N outputs from one slot and is on no list in `SignalNodes`, so no document can build one (LIFE-675). The slices are the animation's own -- its ten log-spaced bands over bins 1-256 cut three ways, [0,2] [3,5] [6,9], which is bins 1-4, 5-27 and 28-256. Per-band auto-gain comes free: `audio_band` IS prism_line's gain staging, so each slice is normalised against its own rolling maximum and bass no longer swamps treble.\n\n`phase_spread` is 0, which is the animation at rest and what makes this one path rather than three. Above 0 it spreads the colours evenly around the cycle -- reachable only by giving each layer its own LFO at one rate with fixed phase offsets, which is what `showcase/21-prism-fan` is.\n\nWHAT HAS NO KNOB AND WHY: `len_max`, `amp_min`, `amp_max` and `freq_max` are row DEPTHS and a depth has no address; `brightness` is the glow row's depth for the same reason, so `floor` -- its base -- is the knob that pair gets. `fall` is the animation's asymmetric peak envelope, which `audio_band` has no attack/release split for. `band_low`/`band_high` would have to re-cut three slices from one pair of numbers. `split`, the on/off, is a toggle; `split_depth` at 0 is the same thing.",
